{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0197oRW5aeGD41eo14pdYYum","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"latest stable Rust release blog.rust-lang.org announcing Rust 1.\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Rust Release Announcements\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/releases/\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Rust 1.96.0\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/05/28/Rust-1.96.0/\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Rust 1.98.0\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/08/20/Rust-1.98.0/\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Rust 1.0\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2015/05/15/Rust-1.0/\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Rust 1.88.0\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/06/26/Rust-1.88.0/\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Rust 1.86.0\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/04/03/Rust-1.86.0/\"},{\"title\":\"Rust 1.1 stable, the Community Subteam, and RustCamp\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2015/06/25/Rust-1.1/\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Rust 1.97.0\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/07/09/Rust-1.97.0/\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Rust 1.97.1\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/07/16/Rust-1.97.1/\"},{\"title\":\"Announcing Rust 1.84.0\",\"url\":\"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/01/09/Rust-1.84.0/\"}]\n\nThe latest stable release I found is **Rust 1.99.0**, announced on October 1, 2026, according to the Rust release announcements index. Releases in 2026 include Oct. 1 · Announcing Rust 1.99.0, Sept. 3 · Announcing Rust 1.98.1, and Aug. 20 · Announcing Rust 1.98.0. I could not retrieve the 1.99.0 post itself, so I have no details of its contents. The only source for that release is the index listing.\n\nThe most recent release post I could read is for **Rust 1.98.0**. Its highlights included new algebraic floating-point methods, which let f32 and f64 perform addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, and remainder with algebraic optimizations. It also added a format_into method on all primitive integer types, which takes a buffer large enough to hold the decimal form of any value of that type.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ebb9655-8320-4a67-961e-ed4a1999a910","uuid":"0d8a8c3b-6ca4-45b4-8d4d-e728fe160858","timestamp":"2026-10-17T02:40:19.026Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"latest stable Rust release blog.rust-lang.org announcing Rust 1.","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01XHrJWVzVge6D5E2v1w5A1G","content":[{"title":"The Rust Release Announcements","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/releases/"},{"title":"Announcing Rust 1.96.0","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/05/28/Rust-1.96.0/"},{"title":"Announcing Rust 1.98.0","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/08/20/Rust-1.98.0/"},{"title":"Announcing Rust 1.0","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2015/05/15/Rust-1.0/"},{"title":"Announcing Rust 1.88.0","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/06/26/Rust-1.88.0/"},{"title":"Announcing Rust 1.86.0","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/04/03/Rust-1.86.0/"},{"title":"Rust 1.1 stable, the Community Subteam, and RustCamp","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2015/06/25/Rust-1.1/"},{"title":"Announcing Rust 1.97.0","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/07/09/Rust-1.97.0/"},{"title":"Announcing Rust 1.97.1","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/07/16/Rust-1.97.1/"},{"title":"Announcing Rust 1.84.0","url":"https://blog.rust-lang.org/2025/01/09/Rust-1.84.0/"}]},"The latest stable release I found is **Rust 1.99.0**, announced on October 1, 2026, according to the Rust release announcements index. Releases in 2026 include Oct. 1 · Announcing Rust 1.99.0, Sept. 3 · Announcing Rust 1.98.1, and Aug. 20 · Announcing Rust 1.98.0. I could not retrieve the 1.99.0 post itself, so I have no details of its contents. The only source for that release is the index listing.\n\nThe most recent release post I could read is for **Rust 1.98.0**. Its highlights included new algebraic fl